# The `github` tool (design/agent-github.md, "PRs"): the std/go worker image with
# this directory's program curried onto it, plus the `help` it is described by.
# A reader with no `@in`: its ArgTree is its arguments and nothing else, so
# `@call` adds the tool call's id to make each call its own run. A caller
# outside llm-step passes `--call=<any unused value>` itself.
HELP=<<END
Call the GitHub API at api.github.com, with the granted github-token: everything
about a PR except its commits, which publish_source pushes. Find a branch's open
PR, open one, change its base, link PRs as a stack. Nothing is checked out.

The result is the HTTP status line, then the response body, cut if long. A
response of any status is a result; the run fails only when none came back,
and then a write may still have arrived: read the affected state with a GET
before sending it again.

@param method GET, POST, PATCH, PUT or DELETE.
@param path API path with any query string, such as /repos/owner/repo/pulls?head=owner:branch&state=open. GraphQL is POST /graphql.
@param [body] JSON request body, such as {"title":"Add the parser","head":"parser","base":"main","body":"Why."}.
@call
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/go --worker1:@=worker.go --help=$HELP
